#: matesla/poll_diagnostics.py:329
msgid ""
"Habit model is trusted. For idle/asleep hours it can set 5, 15 or 30 minute "
"spacing from historical weekday+hour patterns. Live drive, charge and cabin "
"activity always keep the short reactive intervals."
msgstr ""
"Het gewoonte-model is betrouwbaar. Bij idle/slaap kan het 5, 15 of 30 "
"minuten zetten uit historische weekdag+uur-patronen. Rijden, laden en cabine"
" houden altijd de korte reactieve intervallen."

#: matesla/poll_diagnostics.py:334
msgid "No VIN is available, so habit-based spacing cannot run."
msgstr "Geen VIN beschikbaar, dus spacing op gewoontes kan niet draaien."

#: matesla/poll_diagnostics.py:337
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Not enough reference weeks of telemetry before the last %(recent)s days "
"(have %(have)s, need at least %(need)s). Capture uses only the default "
"day/night spacing until history is long enough."
msgstr ""
"Niet genoeg referentieweken telemetrie vóór de laatste %(recent)s dagen (heb"
" %(have)s, minstens %(need)s nodig). Capture gebruikt alleen de standaard "
"dag/nacht-afstand tot er genoeg historie is."

#: matesla/poll_diagnostics.py:348
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Recent mobility does not match the reference weeks (regime break). Habits "
#| "are disabled so a school↔holiday or trip change cannot stretch polls "
#| "incorrectly. Baseline day/night spacing is used until patterns look "
#| "consistent again."
msgid ""
"Recent mobility does not match the reference weeks (regime break). Habits "
"are disabled so a school↔holiday or trip change cannot stretch polls "
"incorrectly. Default day/night spacing is used until patterns look "
"consistent again."
msgstr ""
"Recente mobiliteit komt niet overeen met de referentieweken (regime-breuk). "
"Gewoontes zijn uitgeschakeld zodat school↔vakantie of een reis polls niet "
"fout uitrekt. Baseline dag/nacht geldt tot patronen weer consistent lijken."

#: matesla/poll_diagnostics.py:355
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "There are enough reference weeks, but no weekday+hour slot was classified "
#| "quiet, moderate or busy. Baseline spacing only."
msgid ""
"There are enough reference weeks, but no weekday+hour slot was classified "
"quiet, moderate or busy. Default spacing only."
msgstr ""
"Er zijn genoeg referentieweken, maar geen weekdag+uur-slot is stil, matig of"
" druk geclassificeerd. Alleen baseline-spacing."

#: matesla/poll_diagnostics.py:358
#, fuzzy, python-format
#| msgid ""
#| "Habit model is not trusted (%(reason)s). Baseline spacing only."
msgid "Habit model is not trusted (%(reason)s). Default spacing only."
msgstr ""
"Gewoonte-model is niet betrouwbaar (%(reason)s). Alleen baseline-spacing."

#: matesla/poll_diagnostics.py:370
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Recent mobile hours per day dropped sharply versus the reference period "
"(typical of school → holiday). Detail: %(detail)s"
msgstr ""
"Mobiele uren per dag daalden sterk t.o.v. de referentieperiode (typisch "
"school → vakantie). Detail: %(detail)s"

#: matesla/poll_diagnostics.py:375
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Recent mobile hours per day rose sharply versus the reference period "
"(typical of holiday → school or a trip). Detail: %(detail)s"
msgstr ""
"Mobiele uren per dag stegen sterk t.o.v. de referentieperiode (typisch "
"vakantie → school of reis). Detail: %(detail)s"

#: matesla/poll_diagnostics.py:380
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Several recent drives occurred in weekday+hour slots that were historically "
"almost never mobile. Detail: %(detail)s"
msgstr ""
"Meerdere recente ritten vielen in weekdag+uur-slots die historisch bijna "
"nooit mobiel waren. Detail: %(detail)s"

#: matesla/poll_diagnostics.py:416
msgid "night"
msgstr "nacht"

#: matesla/poll_diagnostics.py:416
msgid "day"
msgstr "dag"

#: matesla/poll_diagnostics.py:422
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Driving with navigation ETA %(eta)s min → query every %(minutes)s min (2 min"
" near arrival or when crawling; %(mid)s min mid-trip; %(far)s min when ETA "
"is long). Habits do not apply while driving."
msgstr ""
"Rijden met navigatie-ETA %(eta)s min → query elke %(minutes)s min (2 min "
"dicht bij aankomst of kruipend; %(mid)s min mid-trip; %(far)s min bij lange "
"ETA). Gewoontes gelden niet tijdens rijden."

#: matesla/poll_diagnostics.py:433
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Driving without navigation ETA → dense %(minutes)s min queries (stretch only"
" when Tesla reports minutes-to-arrival). Habits do not apply while driving."
msgstr ""
"Rijden zonder navigatie-ETA → dichte queries elke %(minutes)s min (rekken "
"alleen als Tesla aankomstminuten geeft). Gewoontes gelden niet tijdens "
"rijden."

#: matesla/poll_diagnostics.py:439
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Live activity “%(activity)s” → reactive default spacing %(minutes)s min "
"(%(day_or_night)s). Habits do not apply while the car is active."
msgstr ""
"Live-activiteit “%(activity)s” → reactieve standaardafstand %(minutes)s min "
"(%(day_or_night)s). Gewoontes gelden niet terwijl de auto actief is."

#: matesla/poll_diagnostics.py:449
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Idle/asleep policy: habit class “%(habit_class)s” sets %(minutes)s min for "
"this weekday+hour (default would be %(baseline)s min, %(day_or_night)s)."
msgstr ""
"Idle/slaap-beleid: gewoonteklasse “%(habit_class)s” zet %(minutes)s min voor"
" deze weekdag+uur (standaard zou %(baseline)s min zijn, %(day_or_night)s)."

#: matesla/poll_diagnostics.py:459
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Idle/asleep policy: slot is historically moderate, but at night moderate "
"does not densify — keep night default %(minutes)s min."
msgstr ""
"Idle/slaap-beleid: slot is historisch matig, maar ’s nachts verdicht matig "
"niet — nachtstandaard %(minutes)s min blijft."

#: matesla/poll_diagnostics.py:463
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Idle/asleep policy: no habit for this weekday+hour → %(day_or_night)s "
"default %(minutes)s min."
msgstr ""
"Idle/slaap-beleid: geen gewoonte voor deze weekdag+uur → "
"%(day_or_night)s-standaard %(minutes)s min."

#: matesla/poll_diagnostics.py:754
msgid ""
"Forecast and week grid describe idle/asleep/sentry spacing only. If the car "
"drives, DC/AC charges or has cabin activity, capture switches to the short "
"reactive default until that ends."
msgstr ""
"Voorspelling en weekraster beschrijven alleen idle/slaap/sentry-afstand. Als"
" de auto rijdt, (DC/AC) laadt of cabine-activiteit heeft, schakelt capture "
"naar de korte reactieve standaard tot dat stopt."

#: matesla/poll_diagnostics.py:759
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Habits use at most the last %(lookback)s days, require %(min_weeks)s "
"reference weeks before the last %(recent)s days, and disable themselves on a"
" regime break."
msgstr ""
"Gewoontes gebruiken max. de laatste %(lookback)s dagen, vereisen "
"%(min_weeks)s referentieweken vóór de laatste %(recent)s dagen, en schakelen"
" uit bij een regime-breuk."

#: matesla/poll_diagnostics.py:769
#, python-format
msgid ""
"When habits are trusted, every weekday+hour is busy (%(busy)s min), quiet "
"(%(quiet)s min), or moderate (%(moderate)s min by day; night moderate keeps "
"the %(night)s min night default). There is no idle “default hole” in the "
"grid — only untrusted models fall back to day %(day)s / night %(night)s "
"everywhere."
msgstr ""
"Als gewoontes betrouwbaar zijn, is elke weekdag+uur druk (%(busy)s min), "
"stil (%(quiet)s min) of matig (%(moderate)s min overdag; ’s nachts houdt "
"matig de nachtstandaard %(night)s min). Geen standaardafstand-„gat“ — alleen"
" onbetrouwbare modellen vallen overal terug op dag %(day)s / nacht "
"%(night)s."

